WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:02.480
While we were searching for the Number inside the ruins,

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.020
we were reunited with Alit inside
 the submerged Colosseum inside the lake.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.110
After obtaining the Number inside the ruins,

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.150
Alit actually brainwashed Gauche and forced him to Duel us!

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.660
Alit! What in the world happened to you?!

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.120
I'm gonna kick your ass no matter what!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.120
No matter what it takes to do it!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.330
What a Monster Effect he has...!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.080
Yeah...

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.210
Alit...

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:28.800
Be careful, Yuma.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.710
Lion Heart is a Number with the effect to take the damage

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.470
he receives and inflict the damage to the opposing player.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.800
It's powerful, but it requires great risk.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.640
So instead of using it himself,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.020
he brainwashed Gauche and forced him to use it?!

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.270
What's with this light?

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.360
These are...the feelings of people who filled this Colosseum...

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.490
...crossing over time itself!

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.660
I will...end my turn there.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.170
Gauche, I swear I'm gonna bring you back to your senses!

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.250
My turn! Draw!

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.380
I attack Alit's face-down Monster with Hope!

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.180
Too naive, Yuma!

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.600
I activate the effect of Backhand Gardna!

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.390
When this guy is attacked while in Face-Down Defense Position,

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.770
he can switch the attack target to another Monster!

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.230
I switch Hope's attack target to Lion Heart!

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:35.360
And if the one attacking is an Xyz Monster,

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.950
it sends all its Overlay Units to the Graveyard!

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.580
Hope's Overlay Units?!

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:42.990
This is bad, Yuma!

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.250
That's right! It all ends for you two!

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.040
Do it, knucklehead!

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.340
I activate Lion Heart's effect!

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.010
When this card is destroyed by battle,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.840
I can instead inflict the same damage I take to the opposing player!

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.800
Burning Cross Counter!

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.310
They'll both take 2400 points of damage!

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.310
He's aiming for a double knockout?!

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.320
Farewell, Yuma! Astral!

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:44.810
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.850
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:55.320
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.860
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:03.740
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:10.080
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.290
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:16.170
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.800
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.890
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:32.350
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.920
"Be Revived!
 The Duelist Soul That Transcends Life!!"

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.790
Trap, activate! Phantom Butterfly Protection!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.840
It halves the damage an ally player takes!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.290
Droite!

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.260
Gauche!

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:14.480
I feel bad for Gauche,
 but Yuma and Droite will definitely win this.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.360
Gauche!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.190
Not yet!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.570
Lion Heart has another effect!

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:24.450
When a player's Life hits zero because of battle damage,

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:30.450
by detaching one Overlay Unit,
 I can raise that Life from 0 to 100!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.000
Lion Heart! Rescue Shock!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.050
G...Gauche!

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.840
As long as that Number has Overlay Units,

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.260
players can be revived and forced to continue fighting?!

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:54.890
That's right. But the one who uses it 
will be beaten to the edge of death.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.020
Alit... damn you!

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.440
I activate the other effect of Phantom Butterfly Protection!

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.570
When the battle ends, it switches one of the opponent's Monsters to Defense Position!

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.990
Now I see. Lion Heart's effect to negate destruction

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.660
can only be used when in Attack Position!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.460
If it's in Defense Position, they can beat it down!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.840
I set one card! Turn end!

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.970
Gauche! How long are you going to let that boy do what he likes with you?!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.430
Did you call me boy?!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.010
Gauche! Why do you look so pathetic?!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.810
The Duel you're in right now doesn't have a shred of passion!

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.310
Have you forgotten what your dream is?!

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:40.400
Both your dream and mine...?! Answer me, Gauche!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.650
That's no use. Your voice won't be able to reach him.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.700
My turn! Hah!

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:53.160
Draw!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:57.040
I Summon Burning Knuckler Rabbit Puncher!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:05.050
I Overlay the Level Three Backhand Gardna and Rabbit Puncher!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.970
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.640
Xyz Summon!

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:16.390
Bend all will to your control using your black authority as you enter before us!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.190
Burning Knuckler Cheat Commissioner!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.400
And I use Cheat Commissioner to attack Hope!

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:32.120
He's attacking with a zero Attack Power Monster?!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.080
Don't let your guard down, Yuma!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.660
At this moment, I activate Cheat Commissioner's effect!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.040
When this Monster battles,

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.880
all Monsters on the field switch to Attack Position!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.380
Forced Fighting Pose!

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.940
I activate Cheat Commissioner's other effect!

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:05.900
When an ally Monster on the field
 battles alongside Cheat Commissioner,

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.200
I can switch it with a Monster on my field!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.160
The Monsters switched places!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.370
We've only got 400 Life.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.830
If we take Lion Heart's effect, this time...!

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.210
You said it! This time, it's over for you!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:23.790
Trap, activate!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.050
Imposing Phantom Butterfly!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.670
When the opponent's Monster attacks,

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.760
this card changes the attack target to my field,

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.260
and it to an Attack Position Phantom Butterfly Monster I control!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.270
Bring it, Gauche!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.850
Droite! If you do that, you'll...!

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.650
I activate Lion Heart's Monster Effect!

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.940
Burning Cross Counter!

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.370
Droite!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.590
I'll be all right...

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.050
More importantly, how's Gauche?

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.380
Not done yet! Lion Heart's effect activates!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:17.430
I detach an Overlay Unit to Rescue Shock!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.770
G-Gauche!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:31.900
That's good.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.780
Alit... damn you!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:34.910
Gauche...

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.370
The mood you're in right now...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.960
If you Duel with those half-dead eyes...

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.130
...do you really think you can be a messenger from the stars for those kids?!

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.130
I already <i>told you</i> that your voice won't be able to reach him!

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.260
I set one card face-down to end my turn.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.010
My turn! Draw!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.930
I Summon Phantom Butterfly Assassin Morpho!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.610
Then I Special Summon Phantom Butterfly Assassin Ulysses!

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:12.150
When a Monster is Summoned on my field in Attack Position,

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.900
I can Special Summon her from my hand!

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:21.330
I Overlay the Level Four Swallowtail, Morpho, and Ulysses!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.960
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.500
Xyz Summon!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:31.050
Dance in the darkness, beautiful Incarnation of Death!

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.590
Night Butterfly Assassin!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.430
2600 Attack Points?!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.850
But even if it's got high Attack Power,

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.850
it's all the more disadvantageous with Lion Heart as its opponent.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.810
I then activate the Magic Card, Overlay Capture, from my hand!

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.360
This card steals one Overlay Unit
 from one of the opponent's Monsters,

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.780
and adds it as an Overlay Unit for an Xyz Monster I control!

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.530
Heck yeah!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.200
If Lion Heart loses its Overlay Units,

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.950
he can't use Rescue Shock.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.330
<i>Hang on, Gauche.</i>

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.420
<i>I'll undo the curse he placed on you...</i>

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:11.290
You fool.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:15.010
Trap, activate! Xyz Battle Chain!

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.630
When all of us have Xyz Monsters on the field,

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:24.430
this card negates and destroys any Magic or Trap that targets an Xyz Monster upon activation!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.600
The Overlay Unit...!

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:33.110
Then, if this effect was activated during a turn in which the opponent didn't battle,

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:37.150
the opponent's Xyz Monster and one of my Xyz Monsters

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.820
will be forced to battle each other!

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.070
What did you say?!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.490
I'll start by crushing you first, Droite!

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:48.250
Crap! If she takes the effect of Lion Heart now...

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.170
Droite!

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:54.960
<i>I have nothing in my hand
 that can match this sudden development...</i>

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.010
<i>It pains me to say it, but this seems to be the end for me...</i>

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:01.590
<i>Gauche...</i>

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:08.310
Do it, Lion Heart! Attack Night Butterfly Assassin!

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.610
I activate Night Butterfly Assassin's effect!

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.440
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.570
for each Overlay Unit on the field,

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.160
I increase her Attack Points by 400!

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.790
There are five Overlay Units in total,
 so she gains 2000 points in total!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.290
Fool. Have you lost your mind?

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.540
She's got 4600 Attack Points?!

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.960
Why would she, knowing she'll take all that damage herself?!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.970
Those 4600 Attack Points aren't simply Attack Points.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:40.720
Eh?

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:45.930
In a matter of speaking, they represent Droite trying to reach her feelings to Gauche.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:50.060
Droite is currently willing to punish herself

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.480
if it means getting Gauche's heart back from his brainwashing!

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.270
Go!

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:58.070
I take everything I have and smash it into Gauche!

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:02.450
Reawaken your soul as a Duelist!

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.110
Gauche!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:09.410
Take... everything that I have!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.000
Droite!

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.970
Hey, Droite! Hang in there!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.550
Forgive me, Yuma...

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:27.600
What are you saying, Droite?!

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.890
This is it for me.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:34.140
But my Monster still remains on the field.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:38.820
I leave you with Night Butterfly Assassin.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:39.730
Droite?

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.280
And also, I'm leaving Gauche to you...

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.490
Yuma, I'm sure you... can...

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.660
Hey, Droite! Droite!

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.620
I activate Lion Heart's effect!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.880
I detach one Overlay Unit to Rescue Shock!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:12:59.960
Gauche!

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.220
C'mon, knucklehead! Hurry an' wake up!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.550
D-Damn you!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:13.020
I then activate a Trap! Numbers Overlay Booster!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:16.440
This card, by selecting one Number on the field

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:19.060
when one loses all its Overlay Units,

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.990
I can use two cards from my hand as its Overlay Units!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.660
Now, finish off Yuma this time for good!

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.030
Gauche...

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.790
My turn. Draw!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.000
<i>Oh? He drew Barian's Force?</i>

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.460
<i>Well, using that card won't do much for me at the moment.</i>

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:41.170
Tch, this is bad.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.550
If he keeps using the effect of Lion Heart...

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.510
C'mon, what're you doing?!

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:50.550
Destroy Yuma and Astral with Lion Heart already!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.900
I activate the Equip Magic, Stoic Challenger!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:06.360
This card equips itself to one of my Xyz Monsters and detaches all its Overlay Units,

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.110
and for each Overlay Unit sent to the Graveyard,

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.330
its Attack Points rise by 600!

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:15.500
Also, it doubles all Battle Damage this card dishes out!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.290
Wh-What the hell do you think you're doing?!

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:22.210
However, the Monster equipped with this card will be destroyed during my next turn.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.050
Why did he increase Lion Heart's Attack Power?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:30.050
Next, I equip the Equip Magic, Heroic Growth, to Lion Heart!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.680
When my Life is lower than my opponent's,

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.350
this card doubles the equipped Monster's Attack Power!

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.310
Yuma's only got 400 Life. Gauche has 100.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.270
That means...

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.360
It's higher than Hope's Attack Points!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.280
Gauche...!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:02.710
I see. So that's it.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:06.210
Gauche! Your mood really is the best!

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.510
I attack Hope using Lion Heart!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.980
And because of Stoic Challenger, the damage is doubled.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:23.190
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.650
Unreal! Why's this guy...

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:27.990
That's it, Gauche!

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:33.570
A heated, straightforward match! That's how you fight!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.950
Did the brainwashing ware off?

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:36.700
That's not it.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:37.240
Eh?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.080
Gauche's consciousness is still being controlled.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.080
But because Droite attacked him with all her might,

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.590
she shook his captured soul

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.460
and etched her final impression into him.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.220
She brought back his instinct as a Duelist!

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.890
This! What you see there is a True Duelist!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:56.850
Bring it, Gauche!

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.390
I'll take everything you dish out!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.900
My turn! Draw!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:06.150
Droite, I won't waste your consideration!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.820
I activate the Magic Card, Xyz Shift!

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:14.700
By sending an Xyz Monster from my field to the Graveyard,

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:18.290
I can Special Summon a Monster with the same rank!

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.540
Show yourself, Heroic Champion - Excalibur!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:30.840
And Xyz Shift becomes an Overlay Unit for the Monster it Special Summoned!

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:34.640
Gauche, as proof of our passionate Duel,

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.850
this is the Monster you left me!

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:43.140
I use Excalibur to attack Lion Heart!

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.650
And I activate its Monster Effect at the same time!

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:50.280
By using its Overlay Units, I double its Attack Power during this turn!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.570
I won't let you!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.570
Trap, activate! Battler's Cry!

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.780
When the opposing Monster's Attack Power goes up,

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.910
it doubles the Attack Power of my Monster!

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:07.040
Sweet! Sweet! Things're getting more interesting!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:07.630
Yuma!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.290
Yeah!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.630
Trap, activate! Soul Strike!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.630
When my Life is less than 2000,

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.550
by halving my Life,

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:23.100
during a battle, I can add the same amount of Life I paid to the Attack Power of one Monster!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:27.520
That's useless! That means its Attack Power
 only rises by another 100.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.820
Wh-What's with Lion Heart?!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:37.070
Yuma's true goal was to make his Life equal to Gauche's 100.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.530
What?!

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.620
The Equip Magic, Heroic Growth

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.750
won't activate when both players have the same Life.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:49.630
Lion Heart's Attack Power rises to 1300 because of Stoic Challenger,

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.000
and doubles because of Heroic Growth.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.010
Then Battler's Cry doubles it yet again.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:59.720
But without Heroic Growth's effect, it falls to 2600!

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.220
Th-This can't be!

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:06.600
Go! Finish him off, Excalibur!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.560
Bring it, Yuma!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:15.030
Screw that! I activate Cheat Commissioner's effect!

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:17.530
When a Monster other than this Monster battles,

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:20.030
by detaching all its Overlay Units,

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:22.660
if my opponent has a Magic Card in their hand,

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.660
the battle ends and it can be activated!

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.670
Go on, Gauche! Use that card! Use Barian's Force!

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.380
Yuma, do it now!

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:32.290
Right!

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.590
Trap, activate! Overlay Marker!

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.380
When you battle with this card,

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:43.010
and when an Xyz Monster detaches all its Overlay Units,

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:46.180
it negates that activated effect and destroys it!

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:50.230
And then deals damage to the owner controlling that Xyz Monster

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:54.520
equal to the total Attack Power of the battling Monsters!

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:58.070
I...take 6700 pints worth of damage?!

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.400
Take this, Alit!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.910
Mine and Gauche's heated souls!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:18.800
<i>Th...</i>

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:22.760
<i>These memories...!</i>

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.490
Man... He sure does like keeping us on edge!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.240
Yuma...

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:49.410
Wh-What the hell...?!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.330
What the hell <i>was</i> that just now?!

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:57.670
Alit...

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.680
G-Gauche!

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.810
Hey! Hang in there! Hey!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.400
Just what was I...?

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.110
Ah, here it is!

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:23.570
Dad, you were watching over me this time huh?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:28.540
Stop being so unsociable.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:32.460
Why didn't you tell me that you were
 duking it out with the Barians?

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.500
I'd of helped you beat the hell outta them!

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:36.460
You idiot!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:38.960
You have your dream with Droite!

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.920
Your dream to be the messenger from the stars for these kids!

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.300
Isn't that right, Gauche?

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:45.970
Yuma...

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:49.890
I guess that's right.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:21:05.110
Gauche! Gauche! Gauche!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:57.650
<i>He's done it! Gauche the Starman!</i>

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:02.940
<i>Congratulations on becoming the new Spartan City Champion!</i>

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.660
Gauche the Starman!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.910
- I knew he could!
 - Go!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.080
I wonder if I can become as strong as Gauche the Starman if I work hard enough?!

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:12.000
Yeah!

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.000
Of course you can!

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:19.340
Just like the stars shining brightly in the sky!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.510
Gosh! Why didn't you wake me up?!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.380
I can't believe you actually left me out!

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.720
I'm sorry. I would've felt bad if I woke you up.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.350
But even so...!

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.810
If someone's going to complain, I have the luxury to do so!

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:37.560
I was left alone to watch the ship... I was really lonely!

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:39.900
Yuma.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.190
Are you thinking about Alit?

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.860
Don't you understand after that Duel yesterday?

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.910
In the end, he's a Barian.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:52.700
It's unfortunate, but we cannot exist beside them.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:57.580
<i>Alit... I can't understand why you became that way!</i>

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:00.000
<i>But I believe!</i>

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.960
<i>One of these days, just like before,</i>

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:08.550
<i>we'll have a fair-and-square passionate Duel where we clash our feelings head-on.</i>

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:23.900
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:26.440
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:27.650
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:29.070
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.950
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:34.450
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:37.000
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:38.080
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:39.120
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.500
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:44.840
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:47.970
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:50.180
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:53.180
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.140
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:56.520
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:58.390
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:02.690
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:07.780
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:09.030
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:13.030
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:18.410
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:19.620
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:23.750
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:25.920
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:28.130
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:43.190
The dreamlike mountain that rises to the far distant yonder.

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.480
The fourth ruins we've been searching for lies there.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.360
Hearing the resonating cries of a dragon,

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:51.990
a rigorous trial begins for Kaito!

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:54.120
The Number wants something from me?

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:55.660
That elder of the ruins...!

00:23:55.870 --> 00:23:57.410
I'm not climbing up that thing!

00:23:57.700 --> 00:23:59.080
Just who in the world is he?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.580
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:05.210
"The Trial For Galaxy-Eyes Users! Kaito's Do-Or-Die Duel"

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:07.500
That Number's a Dragon?!
